The original path predicate OriginalControlComposition.OriginalControl enforces the finite-duration, continuity, strict-domain, finite-variation and absolute-continuity/finite-piecewise-$C^1$ conditions described in Section 1. Its concatenation and analytic helpers construct paths, not arbitrary acquisitions or decoders. The original probability–phase controls include $P=\partial_\kappa$ and $Q=\sum_a w_a(\kappa)\partial_{h_a}$ with nonzero double-wall commutator $-(\partial_u+\partial_v)/r$. Probability-changing noncommuting controls prevent treating diagonal filters or a Schur menu as exhaustive native operations. They also do not prove arbitrary instrument enactment. Failure of a particular supplied mechanism is not a global native impossibility theorem.

